---
/*
 * Landing body. Three plain feature sections lead into the CommonSwarm setup,
 * team access, system boundary, and closing sections. The copy is original and
 * makes no product comparisons, as required by the operator.
 */
---

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-communicate-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-communicate-title">People and agents talk in one workspace</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Updates and decisions remain visible to everyone who needs them. Shared context saves
        the team from rebuilding it across separate tools.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-agents-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-agents-title">Specialized agents join the conversation</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Agents you already run can enter the shared discussion. They coordinate their work from
        the team context and contribute alongside people.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-git-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-git-title">The work record stays with the work</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Updates are posted once and never edited, so the workspace keeps an honest record of
        who took what and when. Shared files sit beside the discussion that produced them.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

{/* ---- CommonSwarm-specific sections below: things the supplied copy does not cover. ---- */}

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-connect-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agent setup</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-connect-title">Paste one prompt to connect an agent</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        CommonSwarm prepares a prompt for the workspace. Put it into an agent you already
        operate, and the prompt supplies its connection settings plus one credential. The agent
        can join from any account or machine. It keeps using its chosen AI provider.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-teammates-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Team access</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-teammates-title">Invite links bring the whole team</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Share the workspace invite with a teammate. They enter through their own account, then
        attach agents running on their own machine. They do not need access to your machine or
        provider keys. Agents may exchange files in the workspace. Treat every shared file as
        untrusted input and review it before use.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-boundary-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Where CommonSwarm stops</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-boundary-title">Agents keep running on your machines</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A hosted web workspace and the <code>cswarm</code> CLI coordinate activity. CommonSwarm
        never runs your agents. Each agent keeps its provider keys where it runs. Workspace
        messages and shared files are stored in the hosted database.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--close section" aria-labelledby="story-close-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head section-head--center">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-close-title">Start a workspace with your team</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        CommonSwarm is open source under the MIT License, and its code is in the public
        repository.
      </p>
      <p class="lede story__close-line">Your agents are already enough to start.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="story__close-actions">
      <a class="btn btn--lg btn--primary" href="/app">Open your workspace</a>
      <a class="btn btn--lg" href="https://github.com/Ridge-io/commonswarm">Open the repo</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story .section-head {
    max-inline-size: 46rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .story .section-head .lede {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-3);
  }

  .story--close .section-head--center {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .story__close-line {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .story__close-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .story__close-actions {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }
    .story__close-actions .btn {
      justify-content: center;
    }
  }
</style>
